    "allText": "===ARTICLE 0===\nLudovicCreator\n@LudovicCreator\nI made a 1-minute anime short using only AI tools.\n\nStoryboard → animated clips → score → sound effects → voiceover. No traditional animation software. No studio.\n\nHere's how it came together 🧵\n\nScene 1: I started with a concept. A girl chasing a glowing spirit through neon rain-soaked Tokyo streets. I brainstormed with Firefly AI Assistant\n\nAdobe Firefly generated 10 storyboard frames from text prompts alone. Cel shading, bold ink outlines, cinematic framing.\n\nScene 2: Each frame was animated into a video clip. 10 scenes. 4–8 seconds each.\n\nThe fox spirit got blocked by content filters every time. So I redesigned it as pure light , an indigo-gold orb with trailing ribbons. That version passed. And honestly looked better.\n\nScene 3: Audio built in layers. → Ethereal piano score → Continuous rain ambience → Thunder at the standoff + light explosion → 5 voiceover lines placed at exact timecode.\n\nAll generated. All assembled in a single render.\n\nThe result: \"THE GIRL WHO CHASED LIGHT\"\n\n64 seconds. Full arc. Title card to payoff.\n\nThis post is sponsored by Adobe Firefly through a paid partnership, showcasing my experiences as a Brand Ambassador for their innovative platform. All opinions are my own.\n\nMade entirely with @AdobeFirefly AI tools.\n\n#AdobeFireflyAmbassadors #Ad  #HowToAdobeFirefly\n00:00 / 01:04\nMade with AI\nPaid partnership\n11:00 AM · Sep 14, 2026\n·\n3,457\nViews\n23\n17\n85\n10\n\n===ARTICLE 1===\nLudovicCreator\n@LudovicCreator\nSep 14\nHere you can see the full process I did with the Adobe Firefly AI Assistant\n00:48\n1\n7\n104\n\n===ARTICLE 2===\nLudovicCreator\n@LudovicCreator\nSep 14\nEverything generated I could check it in a Firefly Board and do modifications if needed .\n1\n7\n136\n\n===ARTICLE 3===\nLudovicCreator\n@LudovicCreator\nSep 14\nTry Adobe Firefly at firefly.adobe.com\n00:00 / 01:03\n7\n127\n\n===ARTICLE 4===\nLol\n@Lol_lavie\nSep 14\nC’est bluffant\n2\n2\n42",
