    "allText": "===ARTICLE 0===\nShams\n@ShamsAmin56\nDUST REQUIEM \nSome storms don’t pass. They hunt.\n\nOne man. One machine. One brutal race against the desert.\n\nMade with @lovart_ai - Seedance 2.5 + GPT Image 2.5\n\nPrompt Below\n00:12\nShams\n@ShamsAmin56\nSep 8\nKAGEONI The Crimson Wraith \nEvery strike has weight. Every enemy falls differently.\n\nMade with @lovart_ai Seedance 2.5\n\nProcedural Ragdoll Physics works best on Seedance 2.5.\n\n- Pixel Motion used for ultra slo mo\n- Shuriken Tracking\n\nPrompt below\n00:31\nMade with AI\n4:52 AM · Sep 12, 2026\n·\n3,037\nViews\n40\n8\n78\n22\n\n===ARTICLE 1===\nShams\n@ShamsAmin56\nSep 8\nKAGEONI The Crimson Wraith \nEvery strike has weight. Every enemy falls differently.\n\nMade with @lovart_ai Seedance 2.5\n\nProcedural Ragdoll Physics works best on Seedance 2.5.\n\n- Pixel Motion used for ultra slo mo\n- Shuriken Tracking\n\nPrompt below\n00:31\n\n===ARTICLE 2===\nShams\n@ShamsAmin56\nSep 12\n[REFERENCE 1 — HERO / KAEL VOSS]\nUse the uploaded HERO reference as the exact character throughout.\nPreserve his face, beard, messy dark hair, forehead goggles, shredded tan desert scarf/cape, leather straps, shoulder armor, metal bracer, cargo pants, knee protection and dusty boots.\n\n[REFERENCE 2 — THE JACKAL]\nUse the uploaded CAR reference as the exact vehicle throughout.\nPreserve its armored muscle-car silhouette, exposed supercharger, triple intake pipes, aggressive front ram, roof lights, armored windows, giant off-road tires, external exhausts, rear equipment, flag and weathered metal finish.\n\nNever redesign either reference.\n\nENVIRONMENT:\nHuge empty post-apocalyptic desert, cracked highway, dunes, scattered wreckage, rocky mountains and heat haze under harsh late-afternoon sunlight.\n\nA colossal brown-black sandstorm forms on the horizon and races toward Kael.\n\nSTYLE:\nAAA game cinematic × practical stunt movie × brutal wasteland road chase.\n\nRealistic physics.\nVolumetric dust.\nNatural motion blur.\nHeavy mechanical vibration.\nStrong cinematic contrast.\nFast editorial cutting.\nOccasional slow motion and speed ramps.\n\nEvery major beat MUST use a different camera angle.\n\n==================================================\n00:00–00:12 — HERO + JACKAL IGNITION\n==================================================\n\n00:00–00:01.3 — CALM BEFORE THE STORM\n\nCAMERA:\nExtreme low 24mm ground-level hero shot.\n\nREFERENCE 1 stands beside REFERENCE 2.\n\nThe Jackal fills the background while Kael calmly finishes the last centimeter of a cigar.\n\nHis shredded scarf moves gently in the desert wind.\n\nCamera slowly arcs around Kael from front three-quarter toward profile.\n\nKael takes one final drag.\n\nCLOSE-UP INSERT:\norange cigar ember burns brightly.\n\nKael quietly mutters:\n\n“Too damn quiet.”\n\nSFX:\nsoft wind, cigar crackle, distant metallic rattling.\n\nNo music yet.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n00:01.3–00:02.6 — THE HORIZON\n\nSMASH CUT:\n\n120mm TELEPHOTO SHOT directly toward the horizon.\n\nHeat haze compresses the landscape.\n\nA gigantic wall of dust rises behind distant mountains.\n\nCUT:\n\nOVER-THE-SHOULDER CAMERA behind Kael.\n\nThe storm expands across almost the entire horizon.\n\nCamera performs a slow push past his shoulder toward the storm.\n\nWind suddenly becomes stronger.\n\nKael freezes.\n\nHis scarf begins whipping violently.\n\nCUT TO:\nextreme close-up of Kael's eyes.\n\nReflection of the approaching dust wall visible in his goggles.\n\nKael:\n\n“What the hell is that?”\n\nDeep sub-bass rumble begins.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n00:02.6–00:03.6 — CIGAR THROW\n\nCAMERA:\n85mm side-profile close-up.\n\nKael removes the cigar.\n\nHe stares at the storm for half a beat.\n\nKael:\n\n“Yeah... we're not staying for that.”\n\nHe flicks the cigar away.\n\nSPEED RAMP INTO 40% SLOW MOTION.\n\nMACRO TRACKING CAMERA follows the cigar rotating through the air.\n\nBurning embers separate from it.\n\nCamera RACK FOCUSES from Kael → cigar.\n\nCigar hits the sand.\n\nGROUND MACRO:\nhis boot immediately stomps beside it as he runs past.\n\nWHUMP.\n\nReturn instantly to real-time speed.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n00:03.6–00:04.8 — RUN TO JACKAL\n\nHANDHELD 28mm SIDE TRACKING SHOT.\n\nKael runs toward the driver's door.\n\nHis scarf violently trails behind him.\n\nCamera runs parallel with him.\n\nQuick whip-pan toward the storm.\n\nIt is MUCH closer now.\n\nWhip-pan back.\n\nKael grabs the door handle.\n\nKael:\n\n“Come on, Jackal.”\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n00:04.8–00:05.8 — ENTER\n\nCAMERA:\nLOW CAMERA positioned beside the front wheel looking upward.\n\nKael yanks open the heavy armored door.\n\nDoor swings across foreground.\n\nCamera transitions THROUGH the doorway.\n\nMatch-cut into the cabin as Kael drops into the driver's seat.\n\nHis scarf follows him inside.\n\nHe SLAMS the door.\n\nMETAL:\n\nCLANG!\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n00:05.8–00:06.8 — THE KEY\n\nEXTREME MACRO SHOT.\n\nKael's gloved hand pulls out an old mechanical ignition key.\n\nInsert.\n\nCLICK.\n\nRotate.\n\nStarter motor struggles:\n\nGRR—GRR—GRR—\n\nNothing.\n\nCUT TO KAEL'S FACE.\n\nKael:\n\n“Don't do this to me.”\n\nHe turns it again.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n00:06.8–00:07.8 — JACKAL AWAKENS\n\nENGINE EXPLODES TO LIFE.\n\nROOOOAAARR!\n\nCamera instantly changes to:\n\nENGINE-BAY MACRO.\n\nREFERENCE 2's exact supercharger violently shakes to life.\n\nBelts spin.\n\nIntakes vibrate.\n\nMechanical components begin moving.\n\nCUT INSIDE:\n\nDASHBOARD POV.\n\nAnalog gauges illuminate sequentially.\n\nCLICK.\nCLICK.\nCLICK.\n\nSpeedometer and tachometer perform rapid initialization sweeps.\n\nAmber instrument lights illuminate Kael's face.\n\nKael gives a tiny grin.\n\n“That's my girl.”\n\nMusic starts.\n\nHeavy tribal percussion + industrial bass.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n00:07.8–00:08.7 — THROTTLE\n\nPEDAL CAMERA.\n\nExtreme close-up.\n\nKael's dusty armored boot SLAMS the accelerator.\n\nCUT:\n\nTACHOMETER NEEDLE.\n\nRPM violently climbs.\n\nCUT:\n\nSUPERCHARGER.\n\nIntake shakes.\n\nCUT:\n\nKael gripping the steering wheel.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n00:08.7–00:09.7 — EXHAUST\n\nCAMERA:\nextreme low rear three-quarter shot positioned almost directly beside the exhaust.\n\nBOOM!\n\nJackal's external exhaust erupts with a violent orange flame pulse.\n\nHot gas distorts the image.\n\nDust blasts away from the exhaust.\n\nCamera shakes from the pressure wave.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n00:09.7–00:12.0 — LAUNCH\n\nWHEEL-MOUNTED CAMERA.\n\nRear tire begins rotating.\n\nHalf-second burnout.\n\nSand shoots directly across camera.\n\nCUT TO:\n\nLOW FRONT THREE-QUARTER CAMERA.\n\nJackal's suspension squats under torque.\n\nCUT:\n\nREAR GROUND CAMERA.\n\nThe tires bite.\n\nREFERENCE 2 violently launches forward.\n\nSand explodes backward and temporarily covers the lens.\n\nInside cockpit:\n\nKael looks at the rapidly approaching storm through the mirror.\n\nKael:\n\n“Alright, Jackal... RUN.”\n\nGear shift.\n\nTHUNK.\n\nAt EXACTLY 12 seconds:\n\nFULL THROTTLE.\n\n==================================================\n00:12–00:30 — ESCAPE\n==================================================\n\nFrom this moment onward:\n\nNO STOPPING.\nNO CALM SHOTS.\nNO LONG STATIC SHOTS.\n\nEvery shot increases speed and danger.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n00:12–00:14 — THE CHASE BEGINS\n\nEXTREME WIDE AERIAL SHOT.\n\nCamera starts directly above Jackal.\n\nJackal races along a fractured highway.\n\nCamera rapidly tilts upward—\n\nrevealing the colossal storm chasing it.\n\nThe dust wall should dwarf the vehicle.\n\nCUT:\n\nLONG-LENS SIDE PROFILE.\n\nJackal streaks across frame.\n\nForeground rocks whip past camera creating extreme parallax.\n\nKael over engine noise:\n\n“Come on... faster.”\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n00:14–00:16 — STORM ARRIVES\n\nCAMERA:\nlow frontal pursuit camera moving backward approximately one meter above the road.\n\nJackal charges directly toward lens.\n\nBehind it—\n\nTHE STORM HITS.\n\nThe sky disappears into brown darkness.\n\nSand and debris blast across the highway.\n\nJackal's roof lights automatically ignite.\n\nCUT INSIDE:\n\nCAMERA mounted low on passenger side facing Kael.\n\nKael squints through the windshield.\n\nKael:\n\n“That's not a storm...”\n\nBeat.\n\n“That's a wall.”\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n00:16–00:18 — FIRST OBSTACLE\n\nDRIVER POV.\n\nThrough the dust:\n\nA huge abandoned tanker suddenly appears across the highway.\n\nKael:\n\n“Move!”\n\nSteering wheel snaps sideways.\n\nCUT TO:\n\nTOP-DOWN DRONE CAMERA.\n\nJackal enters a violent high-speed drift.\n\nCUT:\n\nEXTREME LOW SIDE CAMERA.\n\nVehicle slides laterally past the tanker.\n\nOnly centimeters of clearance.\n\nSPEED RAMP:\n100% → 35% → 100%.\n\nAt closest point:\n\nMetal side armor SCRAPES the tanker.\n\nSPARKS explode across frame.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n00:18–00:20 — THROUGH THE DEBRIS\n\nREAR BUMPER CAMERA.\n\nStorm throws debris across the road.\n\nJackal accelerates.\n\nA large sheet of rusted metal flies toward camera.\n\nCUT milliseconds before impact.\n\nFRONT WHEEL CAMERA:\n\nJackal crushes smaller debris beneath the tire.\n\nSuspension violently articulates.\n\nKael:\n\n“Stay together, girl.”\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n00:20–00:22 — COLLAPSING HIGHWAY\n\nAERIAL 45-DEGREE CAMERA.\n\nAhead:\n\nthe highway is fractured.\n\nLarge sections have disappeared beneath dunes.\n\nKael shifts gear.\n\nENGINE SCREAMS.\n\nKael:\n\n“One way out.”\n\nJackal aims directly toward a raised broken section of asphalt.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n00:22–00:24 — JUMP\n\nCAMERA:\nultra-low front tracking angle.\n\nJackal hits the ramp.\n\nSuspension compresses—\n\nTHEN RELEASES.\n\nThe entire vehicle launches into the air.\n\nCUT TO:\n\nULTRA-WIDE SIDE PROFILE.\n\nUse 40% cinematic slow motion.\n\nJackal suspended against the enormous storm.\n\nAll four wheels fully airborne.\n\nScarf visible moving inside the cabin.\n\nDust, stones and fragments float through frame.\n\nCUT TO:\n\nCAMERA BELOW VEHICLE.\n\nJackal flies directly overhead.\n\nDetailed undercarriage crosses camera.\n\nEngine ROARS above lens.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n00:24–00:25.5 — IMPACT\n\nGROUND CAMERA looking directly toward landing zone.\n\nJackal SLAMS onto asphalt.\n\nFront suspension compresses violently.\n\nRear follows.\n\nCamera shakes hard.\n\nDust explodes outward.\n\nInstantly return to full speed.\n\nKael:\n\n“Still with me?”\n\nEngine ROARS in response.\n\nKael grins.\n\n“I'll take that as a yes.”\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n00:25.5–00:27.5 — INTO THE STORM\n\nHOOD-MOUNTED CAMERA facing Kael through windshield.\n\nDust consumes everything behind him.\n\nCUT:\n\nINTERIOR PROFILE.\n\nKael rapidly shifts gear.\n\nCUT:\n\nMACRO TACHOMETER.\n\nNeedle near redline.\n\nCUT:\n\nSUPERCHARGER.\n\nCUT:\n\nSPINNING FRONT WHEEL.\n\nCUT:\n\nEXHAUST FLAME.\n\nUse rhythmic 0.3–0.5 second mechanical inserts synchronized with percussion.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n00:27.5–00:29 — LAST PUSH\n\nDRONE CAMERA races inches above the highway behind Jackal.\n\nCamera rapidly gains on the car.\n\nThen sweeps around the driver's side in ONE fluid 180° orbit until facing the front.\n\nJackal fills frame.\n\nStorm completely dominates background.\n\nKael shouts:\n\n“NOT TODAY!”\n\nHe changes gear.\n\nJackal accelerates again.\n\nMassive exhaust flame.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n00:29–00:30 — FINAL IMAGE\n\nCAMERA immediately pulls vertically upward into an enormous aerial crane shot.\n\nJackal becomes progressively smaller.\n\nA narrow surviving highway stretches toward bright sunlight.\n\nBehind:\n\nthe gigantic storm consumes the desert.\n\nJackal continues racing toward the light.\n\nKael, barely audible beneath the engine:\n\n“Keep running, Jackal.”\n\nMusic peaks.\n\nENGINE ROAR.\n\nSUB-BASS IMPACT.\n\nCUT TO BLACK EXACTLY 00:30.\n\n==================================================\nCAMERA LANGUAGE\n==================================================\n\nConstantly vary perspective:\n\n24mm extreme-low hero angle\n35mm three-quarter orbit\n85mm facial close-up\n100mm cigar macro\n120mm compressed telephoto landscape\nover-the-shoulder\nground-level boot camera\nhandheld side tracking\ndoorway transition camera\ndashboard POV\nignition macro\npedal macro\nengine-bay macro\nexhaust camera\nwheel-mounted camera\nfront pursuit camera\nrear bumper camera\ndriver POV\npassenger-seat profile\ntop-down drone\n45° aerial chase\nhood camera\nundercarriage fly-over\nlong-lens side tracking\n180° moving vehicle orbit\nmassive aerial crane pull-out\n\nDo NOT repeat the same camera framing twice consecutively.\n\nUse foreground objects, vehicle bodywork, doors, dust clouds and whip-pans as natural transitions between shots.\n\nACTION CINEMATOGRAPHY:\nUse short 35–45% slow motion ONLY for:\n• cigar throw\n• tanker near-miss\n• airborne jump\n\nEverything else should feel fast and aggressive.\n\nUse controlled speed ramps entering and exiting slow motion.\n\nAdd realistic lens vibration during engine ignition, acceleration and landing.\n\nUse strong foreground parallax during driving shots.\n\n==================================================\nHERO PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nKael should NOT shout constantly.\n\nVoice:\nlow, gravelly, exhausted, dry confidence.\n\nDialogue must feel spontaneous rather than theatrical.\n\nDialogue sequence:\n\n“Too damn quiet.”\n\n“What the hell is that?”\n\n“Yeah... we're not staying for that.”\n\n“Come on, Jackal.”\n\n“Don't do this to me.”\n\n“That's my girl.”\n\n“Alright, Jackal... RUN.”\n\n“Come on... faster.”\n\n“That's not a storm... that's a wall.”\n\n“Move!”\n\n“Stay together, girl.”\n\n“One way out.”\n\n“Still with me?”\n\n“I'll take that as a yes.”\n\n“NOT TODAY!”\n\n“Keep running, Jackal.”\n\nKeep dialogue short enough that it NEVER interrupts the visual action.\n\n==================================================\nAUDIO\n==================================================\n\nPrioritize:\nsupercharged V8 roar,\nignition starter,\nmetallic dashboard switches,\ngear changes,\nsupercharger whine,\nexhaust backfires,\ntire spin,\ngravel strikes,\nsuspension impacts,\narmor rattling,\nsand hitting metal,\nstorm wind,\ncloth flapping,\ncigar ember crackle.\n\nMusic begins subtly when Jackal starts at 00:07.\n\nBuild into aggressive tribal drums + industrial percussion + distorted low brass.\n\nSynchronize major camera cuts and gear shifts with percussion hits.\n\nAllow the engine to dominate the mix during acceleration.\n\n==================================================\nSTRICT CONTINUITY\n==================================================\n\nREFERENCE 1 = exact Kael Voss in EVERY hero shot.\nREFERENCE 2 = exact Jackal in EVERY vehicle shot.\n\nNever change:\nface,\nhair,\ngoggles,\nclothing,\narmor,\nscarf,\nvehicle silhouette,\ngrille,\nsupercharger,\ntires,\nroof lights,\nexhaust,\narmor placement,\nweathering.\n\nMaintain correct spatial continuity between exterior and interior shots.\n\nNo vehicle morphing.\nNo random weapons.\nNo extra characters.\nNo enemy vehicles.\nNo monsters.\nNo subtitles.\nNo captions.\nNo HUD.\nNo text.\nNo logos.\nNo watermark.\n\nSTRUCTURE:\n00:00–00:12 = cinematic storm discovery + Jackal ignition.\n00:12–00:30 = escalating nonstop escape.\n\nThe final 18 seconds must feel significantly faster, larger and more dangerous than the opening.\nMade with AI\n4\n514\n\n===ARTICLE 3===\nSnow\n@iamrealsnow\nSep 13\nthis is insane\n1\n1\n19",
