    "allText": "===ARTICLE 0===\nLudovicCreator\n@LudovicCreator\nMINIMAX H3 is amazing for text rendering.  The possibilities are really huge 🔥\n\nHere few examples , all videos and prompts in comments 👇\n\nMade in Minimax Design @Hailuo_AI\n\n1/6\n00:44\n11:00 AM · Sep 17, 2026\n·\n731\nViews\n3\n2\n23\n6\n\n===ARTICLE 1===\nLudovicCreator\n@LudovicCreator\n4h\nCreate a premium 10-second cinematic title animation in 16:9 landscape for the exact word “ASCEND”. The word must appear one letter at a time in this order: A, then S, then C, then E, then N, then D. Do not show the complete word at the beginning. Do not reveal multiple letters simultaneously. The only readable on-screen text is ASCEND, with exact spelling, spacing, letter order and clear legibility.\n\nCreate a surreal floating city above a glowing cloud ocean at twilight. The environment is continuously animated: luminous towers rise from floating platforms, transparent buildings assemble, elevated bridges extend between letters, windows pulse softly, clouds drift below, dust and light particles float upward, and warm beams of light move across the architecture. The entire world should feel like it is ascending. Make it imaginative, elegant, mysterious and premium, not chaotic or cartoonish.\n\nTypography and city architecture are one connected system. Use refined geometric uppercase letters with clean terminals, strong proportions, open counters and balanced spacing. Each letter begins as a glowing architectural structure, then settles into a solid dark stone and translucent glass form with warm ivory-gold edges. The letters must remain recognizable as letters while buildings grow from their strokes. Bridges connect neighboring characters without hiding their shapes.\n\nTimeline:\n\n0.0–0.7s: Begin with an almost empty floating platform above the clouds. A distant horizon glows softly while the camera faces upward into the vast sky. Small architectural fragments slowly rise as if gravity is reversing.\n\n0.7–1.8s: The letter A rises from two illuminated towers joined by a high bridge. Its triangular form and open counter must be clearly readable. Buildings grow from its strokes and warm light travels upward along the structure.\n\n1.8–3.0s: The letter S forms beside A as a graceful curved elevated road and luminous architectural ribbon. Keep A stable and readable. A glowing bridge connects A to S while clouds and floating structures continue moving below.\n\n3.0–4.2s: The letter C appears as a large open circular glass-and-stone structure with a clear opening. Keep A and S visible and correctly spaced. The camera begins a smooth forward and upward flight through the floating city.\n\n4.2–5.4s: The letter E assembles from one vertical tower and three precise illuminated platforms. Keep the previous letters unchanged. Add rising windows, suspended walkways and moving light trails.\n\n5.4–6.6s: The letter N rises from two tall towers joined by a diagonal bridge. Its diagonal must remain obvious and readable. All previous letters stay visible and connected into one ascending architectural word.\n\n6.6–7.5s: The final letter D forms from a vertical tower and a curved glowing structure. The camera passes between the letter forms and rises above the cloud layer. Only now reveal the complete word ASCEND, perfectly aligned and readable.\n\nFrom 7.5–8.7s, animate ASCEND as one unified floating city-title. The camera flies upward through the center of the typography, passing beneath bridges and between letter counters. Towers glow, transparent surfaces reflect the sky, and warm light travels from A across to D. Keep every letter solid, readable and correctly spaced.\n\nFrom 8.7–10.0s, resolve into a majestic wide hero view. The complete word ASCEND is centered at approximately 75–85% of the frame width, suspended above the clouds. The city continues gentle motion: buildings pulse, bridges remain connected, windows shimmer, clouds drift and light particles rise. Hold the complete word clearly until the final frame.\n\nVisual style: deep indigo and charcoal sky, soft violet haze, dark stone, transparent smoke-gray glass, warm ivory-gold architectural edges and restrained cyan window lights. Use volumetric rays, atmospheric perspective, cinematic depth of field and smooth controlled camera movement. No storm, rain or lightning imagery. No rapid montage, handheld shake or unreadable speed.\n\nSound design only: no music, vocals or spoken words. Use airy high-altitude ambience, soft architectural tones for each letter formation, delicate bridge-building chimes, gentle glass resonance, subtle rising gravity sounds and one spacious final impact when ASCEND locks into the complete city-title. Keep the sound refined, spacious and dreamlike.\n\nDo not add subtitles, taglines, slogans, numbers, fake labels, interface graphics, random text, extra words, logos, watermarks, duplicated letters, simultaneous reveals, broken spelling, collapsing buildings, chaotic destruction or effects that obscure the exact final word ASCEND.\n2/6\n00:00 / 00:10\n1\n3\n183\n\n===ARTICLE 2===\nLudovicCreator\n@LudovicCreator\n4h\nCreate a premium 10-second cinematic title animation in 16:9 landscape for the exact word “AWAKEN”. This must be a completely new visual concept, unrelated to storms, lightning or electric weather. The letters must appear one by one in this exact order: A, W, A, K, E, N. Do not show the complete word at the beginning and do not reveal multiple letters simultaneously. The complete word becomes readable only after all six individual letters have appeared.\n\nCreate a surreal gravity-defying architectural world: a vast dark museum-like void with floating stone platforms, suspended glass slabs, impossible staircases, drifting dust, slow-moving fragments and warm shafts of light entering from above. The environment must remain continuously animated throughout the shot. Architecture subtly rotates and reconfigures, dust drifts in depth, light beams move across surfaces and small fragments rise upward as if gravity is reversing. Make it elegant, mysterious, imaginative and premium, not cartoonish or chaotic.\n\nTypography: use a monumental refined geometric sans-serif with tall uppercase letters, strong architectural proportions, crisp edges and spacious counters. Each letter begins as a physical architectural structure, then locks into a dark stone and brushed-gold dimensional letter with a warm illuminated edge. Preserve the exact spelling, letter order, proportions, spacing and legibility. Never scramble, melt, duplicate or transform the letters into unrelated symbols.\n\nStart with an empty floating architectural void and a single suspended stone platform. At approximately 0.7 seconds, the platform rotates into position and rises dust forms the first letter A. The A becomes a complete readable dimensional structure with an open counter. Keep it visible.\n\nAt approximately 2.0 seconds, a second floating platform folds and connects like a bridge, revealing W through two descending stone planes and a central illuminated valley. Keep the first A stable and correctly spaced. The architecture continues shifting in the background.\n\nAt approximately 3.4 seconds, a circular glass aperture opens in the air and reveals the second A through warm light and rising dust. Keep both A letters distinct, with the first A and second A correctly positioned in the word AWAKEN. Do not merge them.\n\nAt approximately 4.8 seconds, suspended staircase fragments align into the letter K. Its vertical stem and diagonal arms must be clear and readable. The camera makes a slow controlled lateral move while the existing letters remain stable.\n\nAt approximately 6.1 seconds, a vertical shaft of golden light passes through a floating glass slab and reveals E as three precise horizontal architectural planes. Maintain all previous letters and correct spacing.\n\nAt approximately 7.2 seconds, the final letter N rises from two tall stone columns connected by a diagonal beam. A gentle upward gravity wave lifts dust and small fragments around it. The complete word AWAKEN is now visible for the first time, perfectly aligned and readable.\n\nFrom 7.5 to 8.7 seconds, animate the completed word as one unified architectural title. The camera slowly pushes forward between the letter structures. Floating platforms orbit gently around the word, warm light travels across the stone surfaces, and a few glass reflections sweep through the counters. The letters remain solid, readable and physically grounded in the impossible space.\n\nFrom 8.7 to 10 seconds, the environment settles into a majestic final composition. The complete word AWAKEN is centered at approximately 70–80% of the frame width, suspended above a dark reflective floor with floating architecture behind it. The dust slows, the light beams narrow, the fragments settle into orbit and the title holds clearly until the final frame.\n\nUse a restrained palette of deep charcoal, black stone, warm ivory light, brushed gold and transparent smoke-gray glass. No lightning, thunder, rain, storm clouds, electric bolts, neon colors, rainbow effects or weather imagery. No music, vocals or spoken words. Use only subtle cinematic sound design: low architectural resonance for each letter formation, stone movement, glass resonance, soft dust impacts, a rising gravity hum for the final N and one deep elegant final title impact. Keep the sound spacious and refined, not a trailer boom.\n\nThe only readable on-screen text is “AWAKEN”. Do not add subtitles, slogans, taglines, numbers, fake labels, interface graphics, random letters, extra words, logos, watermarks or decorative text. Maintain one clear letter reveal at a time, continuous animated background motion, premium composition, smooth camera movement, cinematic depth and a strong final readable hold.\n3/6\n00:10\n1\n1\n2\n130\n\n===ARTICLE 3===\nLudovicCreator\n@LudovicCreator\n4h\nCreate a premium 10-second cinematic title animation in 16:9 landscape for the exact word “CHRONOS”. Reveal the letters strictly one at a time in this order: C, then H, then R, then O, then N, then O, then S. Do not show the complete word at the beginning. Do not reveal multiple letters simultaneously. The only readable on-screen text is CHRONOS. Preserve exact spelling, letter order, spacing, proportions and legibility.\n\nCreate a visually imaginative time-traveling typography concept. The scene moves through different eras in one continuous transformation: ancient carved stone, illuminated medieval manuscript, industrial brass machinery, early cinema film, modern glass architecture and a luminous near-future space. Each letter is born from a different historical material, then transitions through time into the next material. The background must remain animated: dust moves through ancient light, ink flows across parchment, gears rotate, film strips flutter, glass reflections shift and futuristic particles drift. Do not treat the eras as disconnected random shots; use one continuous golden temporal ribbon that carries the camera and typography through time.\n\nTypography: premium monumental uppercase display lettering with clean geometric structure, strong proportions, open counters, crisp edges and controlled spacing. Each letter must remain clearly recognizable while changing material. The final letters become elegant brushed brass, dark graphite and translucent glass with a warm golden temporal edge. Never scramble, duplicate, melt or replace any letter.\n\nTIMELINE:\n\n0.0–0.8s: Begin in a dark timeless void with a slow rotating golden thread of light and floating dust. No readable text yet. The thread opens an ancient stone chamber.\n\n0.8–2.0s: The letter C is carved into a monumental stone arch. Fine dust falls from the grooves and warm sunlight moves across the carving. C becomes complete and readable. The golden time ribbon passes through its opening.\n\n2.0–3.1s: The letter H appears as illuminated ink on aged parchment, with manuscript strokes and subtle candlelight. Keep C visible as a stone form while the material transition carries the camera forward. H must remain clean and readable.\n\n3.1–4.2s: The letter R assembles from rotating brass gears and clockwork parts in an industrial time-machine chamber. Its vertical stem, bowl and diagonal leg must be clear. Keep C and H stable and correctly spaced.\n\n4.2–5.3s: The first O forms as a circular early-cinema film reel and glowing projection aperture. Film strips move through the background and the O counter remains open and readable.\n\n5.3–6.3s: The letter N constructs from modern steel beams and transparent glass planes in a clean architectural space. A moving reflection travels across its diagonal. Keep all previous letters visible.\n\n6.3–7.1s: The second O appears as a luminous circular portal made from layered glass and clock rings. It must remain a distinct O, not merge with the first O. The golden temporal ribbon now connects the complete sequence.\n\n7.1–7.8s: The final letter S forms from futuristic particles and precise golden light strokes, then settles into a polished glass-and-brass letter. Only now reveal the complete word CHRONOS for the first time.\n\nFrom 7.8–8.8s, animate the complete word CHRONOS as one unified timeline title. The camera flies smoothly through the letters from ancient stone to futuristic glass, while each letter briefly retains a trace of its origin material. A golden temporal ribbon travels from C to S, connecting the letters. The word remains fully readable and correctly spaced.\n\nFrom 8.8–10.0s, resolve into a majestic final composition: the complete word CHRONOS centered at approximately 75–85% of the frame width in a dark museum-like temporal chamber. Ancient stone fragments, parchment fibers, brass gears, film strips, glass architecture and futuristic particles orbit in a restrained layered background. All eras coexist elegantly. The letters settle into a unified premium material: dark graphite, brushed brass, translucent glass and warm gold edge light. Hold the exact word sharply until the final frame.\n\nCamera: begin with a slow macro drift through dust, track forward through the ancient arch, glide over parchment, orbit the brass mechanism, pass through the film-reel O, fly through the glass architecture and finish with a smooth centered hero view. Use continuous match transitions based on circular shapes, vertical strokes and the golden temporal ribbon. No rapid montage, handheld shake or unreadable camera movement.\n\nColor and lighting: ancient amber sunlight, parchment cream, oxidized brass, charcoal graphite, muted film sepia, cool architectural glass and restrained futuristic gold. Use cinematic volumetric rays, realistic material transitions, depth of field and elegant temporal motion. No rainbow effects, cartoon style or chaotic science-fiction visuals.\n\nSound design only: no music, vocals or spoken words. Use distant ancient room resonance, stone dust movement, parchment and ink sounds, precise clockwork ticks, brass gear rotation, film projector flutter, glass resonance, a rising temporal pulse and one deep refined impact when CHRONOS becomes complete. Keep every sound synchronized to the corresponding letter and era, spacious and premium rather than aggressive.\n\nDo not add subtitles, slogans, taglines, numbers, dates, fake labels, interface graphics, extra words, random letters, logos, watermarks, duplicated letters, simultaneous reveals, broken spelling, disconnected era changes, melting typography or effects that obscure the final word CHRONOS.\n4/6\n00:00 / 00:10\n1\n1\n102\n\n===ARTICLE 4===\nLudovicCreator\n@LudovicCreator\n4h\nCreate a premium 10-second cinematic title animation in 16:9 landscape for the exact word “FORGE”. Reveal the letters strictly one at a time in this order: F, then O, then R, then G, then E. Do not show the complete word at the beginning. Do not reveal multiple letters simultaneously. The only readable on-screen text is FORGE. Preserve exact spelling, letter order, spacing, proportions and legibility.\n\nCreate a high-end liquid-metal alchemy world: a black reflective obsidian surface inside a vast dark industrial chamber, glowing molten metal flowing like a living river, slow sparks, floating metallic droplets, heated vapor, smoke and subtle furnace light. The background must remain continuously animated throughout the video: molten streams flow, sparks drift, vapor curls, reflections move and heat pulses travel through the environment. Make it luxurious, powerful and cinematic, not dirty or chaotic.\n\nTypography: use a bold premium geometric uppercase display style with strong clean forms, open counters, crisp edges and balanced spacing. Each letter is forged from liquid chrome and molten silver, beginning as flowing metal, then cooling into a polished steel structure with dark graphite shadows and bright reflective highlights. The letters must remain recognizable throughout formation. Do not melt, scramble, duplicate or distort them into unreadable shapes.\n\nTimeline:\n\n0.0–0.8s: Begin with an empty black obsidian surface. A thin stream of molten silver flows across the frame while furnace glow and smoke create depth. No readable text yet.\n\n0.8–2.0s: Molten metal rises and forms the letter F. Its vertical stem and two horizontal bars become clear. The F cools from orange-white heat into polished chrome and remains fully readable.\n\n2.0–3.3s: A circular pool of liquid chrome coils beside F and solidifies into the letter O. Keep F stable and visible. The O must have a clean open counter with bright inner reflections.\n\n3.3–4.6s: A vertical metal column and curved molten arc form R. Its bowl and diagonal leg must be clearly readable. Keep F and O unchanged while sparks and heated vapor move in the background.\n\n4.6–5.9s: A rotating ring of molten metal forms G, leaving a precise opening and inner horizontal bar. The letter cools into the same polished metallic material. Maintain correct spacing across F, O, R and G.\n\n5.9–7.1s: The strongest controlled metal pour creates E from one vertical beam and three horizontal molten bars. The metal flashes hot, then cools into chrome. Only now is the complete word FORGE visible for the first time.\n\nFrom 7.1–8.5s, animate the complete word FORGE as one unified metallic title. A controlled camera push moves across the reflective surfaces. A bright heat line travels from F to E, reflections ripple across the polished letters, molten metal flows briefly around their bases and a few sparks rise upward. Keep the entire word readable and do not break the letters apart.\n\nFrom 8.5–10.0s, resolve into a premium frontal hero composition. The complete word FORGE is centered at approximately 75–85% of the frame width on the black obsidian surface. The letters are polished dark chrome with silver highlights, subtle warm reflections and a faint orange glow along the lower edges. Molten streams continue moving behind the title, vapor drifts slowly, sparks fade and the reflection remains visible. Hold the exact word sharply until the final frame.\n\nLighting and materials: deep black background, liquid chrome, polished steel, graphite shadows, silver-white highlights, restrained molten orange and dark copper heat. Use realistic reflections, refraction, glowing edges, shallow depth of field, macro metal detail and controlled volumetric smoke. No rainbow chrome, no neon colors, no cartoon effects and no random text.\n\nCamera: begin close to the obsidian surface, track smoothly alongside each forming letter, make one subtle orbit during the final metal pour, then finish in a clean frontal hero view. The camera movement must support readability. No handheld shake, rapid montage or aggressive zoom.\n\nSound design only: no music, vocals or spoken words. Use deep furnace ambience, liquid-metal flow, precise metallic impacts for each letter formation, cooling-metal ticks, short spark crackles, one resonant final forge strike when FORGE becomes complete and a low fading industrial hum. Keep the sound premium and restrained, not a trailer boom.\n\nDo not add subtitles, slogans, taglines, numbers, fake labels, interface graphics, extra words, random letters, logos, watermarks, duplicated letters, simultaneous reveals, broken spelling, melting typography that loses legibility or effects that obscure the final word FORGE.\n5/6\n00:00 / 00:10\n1\n1\n138\n\n===ARTICLE 5===\nLudovicCreator\n@LudovicCreator\n4h\nCreate a premium 10-second cinematic title animation in 16:9 landscape for the exact word “SURGE”. The letters must appear strictly one by one in this order: S, then U, then R, then G, then E. Do not show the complete word at the beginning. Do not reveal multiple letters at the same time. The final complete word SURGE becomes readable only after all five individual letter reveals are finished.\n\nAnimate the storm environment continuously throughout the entire video: dark charcoal thunderclouds rolling and changing, falling rain in layered depth, drifting mist, distant lightning, wet reflective ground, moving cloud light and charged atmospheric particles. The background must remain alive and cinematic, never static.\n\nStart with an empty storm chamber and a faint central glow. At 0.8 seconds, a narrow lightning bolt strikes the first position and electrically traces the letter S into existence. The S forms from silver-white energy filaments, then settles into a dark graphite dimensional letter with a sharp silver rim. Hold it clearly readable.\n\nAt 2.2 seconds, a second electrical pulse travels through the storm and reveals U in the next position. U forms from two descending lightning branches connected by a glowing curve. Keep S visible and stable. Clouds and rain continue moving behind both letters.\n\nAt 3.8 seconds, a controlled lightning strike reveals R. Trace its vertical stem, bowl and diagonal leg with electric energy, then settle it into the same premium material. Keep S and U visible, correctly spaced and unchanged.\n\nAt 5.4 seconds, a stronger storm pulse reveals G. The G forms from a circular electric arc with a precise open gap and horizontal inner stroke. Maintain clear letter identity and keep the existing letters stable. Add subtle reflections on the wet floor.\n\nAt 6.9 seconds, the strongest controlled lightning event reveals E. The E appears through three converging electrical strokes and settles into the same dark graphite and silver-edged material. Only now is the full word SURGE visible. All letters must be correctly spelled, evenly spaced, aligned and fully readable.\n\nFrom 7.4 to 8.7 seconds, animate the completed word SURGE as one unified title. Push the camera forward slightly, let one silver-white lightning rim travel across the letters, form a restrained red-orange energy line beneath the word and intensify the wet-floor reflection. The word may expand slightly toward camera, but never scramble, melt, split or replace any letter.\n\nFrom 8.7 to 10 seconds, calm the storm while keeping the background gently animated. Resolve to a premium frontal hero composition with the complete SURGE centered at approximately 70–80% of the frame width. Keep rolling clouds, light rain, mist, fading lightning and a subtle reflection. Hold the exact word clearly until the final frame.\n\nTypography: premium modular geometric sans-serif, strong uppercase letters, slightly condensed proportions, heavy weight, crisp straight terminals, open counters and subtle dimensional bevels. Letter bodies are dark graphite with silver-white edge highlights. Use electric blue-white lightning for the reveal energy and a restrained red-orange line only as the final underline. Make the design elegant, powerful and high-end, with clean negative space and controlled VFX.\n\nCamera: begin wide and low, slowly push through rain haze, keep the letter positions stable in a central composition, then finish in a clean frontal hero view. Use realistic cinematic depth of field and atmospheric perspective. No handheld shake, rapid montage or movement that reduces readability.\n\nSound design only: no music, vocals, chanting or advertising sting. Use continuous quiet rain, distant rolling thunder, one distinct electrical crackle or lightning impact for each letter reveal, a stronger thunder impact for the E reveal and completed word, then a soft fading rain tail. Synchronize every sound with its visible letter event.\n\nThe only readable on-screen text is “SURGE”. Do not add subtitles, taglines, slogans, numbers, fake labels, interface graphics, random letters, extra words, watermarks, logos, rainbow neon, cartoon lightning, excessive strobe, duplicated letters, simultaneous letter reveals or effects that obscure the final word.\n6/6\n00:00 / 00:10\n1\n1\n173\n\n===ARTICLE 6===\nPromptlyAI\n@PromptlyAI_YT\n3h\nVery nice! 😎\n1\n11",
