    "allText": "===ARTICLE 0===\nLarus Canus\n@MrLarus\n🖤 Typography can completely change the mood of a portrait!\n\nPlaying with giant type, outlines, negative space, and small color accents.\n\n1. SILENCE, negative space\n2. OFFLINE, broken type\n3. RESET, type as a doorway\n4. BREATHE, outline type\n\n✨ Great for fashion editorials, posters, campaigns, and experimental visuals.\n\nPrompt below ↓\nLarus Canus\n@MrLarus\nSep 9\n🤯 Floating glass can completely reshape an editorial portrait!\n\nIt frames the face, bends the type, and pulls the product into the composition.\n\n1. Afterimage, floating prism trail\n2. Light Trace, optical rings\n3. Prism View, refracted lens slices\n4. Hydro Memory, soft hydro lenses\n\nPerfume, jewelry, eyewear, skincare. Same idea, very different results.\n\nPrompt in replies 👇\nMade with AI\n8:45 AM · Sep 17, 2026\n·\n2,623\nViews\n3\n5\n32\n19\n\n===ARTICLE 1===\nLarus Canus\n@MrLarus\nSep 9\n🤯 Floating glass can completely reshape an editorial portrait!\n\nIt frames the face, bends the type, and pulls the product into the composition.\n\n1. Afterimage, floating prism trail\n2. Light Trace, optical rings\n3. Prism View, refracted lens slices\n4. Hydro Memory, soft hydro lenses\n\nPerfume, jewelry, eyewear, skincare. Same idea, very different results.\n\nPrompt in replies 👇\n\n===ARTICLE 2===\nLarus Canus\n@MrLarus\n6h\nPrompt:\n\n[THEME / MAIN WORD]: {SILENCE / OFFLINE / RESET / BREATHE}\n[SHORT MESSAGE]: {e.g. LESS NOISE. MORE SIGNAL.}\n[SUBJECT]: {adult East Asian man / woman}\n[POSE]: {standing / seated / walking / expressive movement}\n[TYPE MECHANISM]: {negative space / broken type / type doorway / expanded outline type}\n[BACKGROUND]: {warm ivory / cool gray / deep navy / charcoal}\n[ACCENT COLOR]: {electric blue / signal red / lime / icy blue}\n[ACCENT LABEL]: {QUIET / AGAIN / DISCONNECT / INHALE}\n[ASPECT RATIO]: 9:16\n\nCreate a high-end fashion editorial portrait poster where the subject and typography share the same visual space rather than looking like text placed over a photo.\n\nUse one adult fashion subject with a clean elongated silhouette, realistic skin and hair, monochrome clothing, natural fabric folds, dimensional studio lighting, and a restrained editorial pose.\n\nBuild the composition around oversized ultra-condensed sans-serif typography. The main word should be extremely large, partially cropped, and function like an architectural element.\n\nCombine bold solid type, thin outline type, cropped letterforms, and clear foreground/background overlaps. Let some letters sit behind the subject while selected outlines or shapes pass in front to create real depth.\n\nUse [TYPE MECHANISM] as the main visual idea:\n• Negative space: typography disappears inside a clean geometric zone around the subject.\n• Broken type: split the word with a deliberate gap and place the subject inside it.\n• Type doorway: turn giant letters into walls or a passage around the subject.\n• Expanded outline type: use widely spaced outline letters and generous negative space.\n\nKeep the background minimal. Add only a few meaningful pieces of microcopy and one small high-saturation [ACCENT COLOR] label containing [ACCENT LABEL].\n\nMaintain a strong hierarchy: one dominant typographic gesture, one subject, one secondary outline layer, one small color accent, and controlled negative space.\n\nThe final image should feel like contemporary fashion editorial art direction: minimal, bold, graphic, photographic, spatial, and stop-scroll worthy.\n331\n\n===ARTICLE 3===\nHeyAnuu\n@theanu_Sayss\n5h\nTypography and negative space add such a strong editorial identity to these portraits.\n1\n16",
